    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk if \"healing\" is even a thing for someone like me. it's not just being sad... it's like the social version of me, the one that had value, is just completely erased. everyone has moved on to the next thing and im just stuck in this weird void. it feels more like a permanent state than just a phase. like there's nothing left to actually rebuild.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Grief does not always leave permanent marks; giving your present self space and permission to rest is the strongest act of self-love you can practice. Trust that your value did not vanish, even when your pain made the world feel unrecognizable, and small, manageable moments of connection can create tangible bridges over this fog. Healing is rarely a straight line toward a fixed destination, but the courage to simply witness your own struggle without judgment often sparks the very resilience you feel is lost.",
      "source": "target",
